title Placing an order and paying online

User [icon: user]
Checkout page [icon: layout]
Orders API [icon: server]
Order ops [icon: shield]
SQLite [icon: database]
Payment modal [icon: credit-card]
Mock gateway [icon: zap]
Webhook handler [icon: webhook]
Mailer [icon: mail]

// ---- 1. create the order (stock is reserved atomically) ----
User > Checkout page: choose address, email, payment method
Checkout page > Orders API: POST /orders items id and qty, coupon, email
Orders API > Order ops: expire stale unpaid orders
Orders API > Orders API: re-validate coupon and compute totals from server prices
Orders API > Order ops: reserve stock UPDATE WHERE stock >= qty

alt [not enough stock] {
  Order ops --> Orders API: out of stock
  Orders API > SQLite: ROLLBACK
  Orders API --> Checkout page: 409 sold out
}
else [stock reserved] {
  Orders API > SQLite: COMMIT order and items
  Orders API --> Checkout page: 201 order with payment_status pending
}

// ---- 2. pay: the browser is NOT trusted, the signed webhook is ----
Checkout page > Payment modal: open the payment window
Payment modal > Orders API: POST /payments/intents
Orders API > SQLite: INSERT payment_intent amount from the order
Orders API --> Payment modal: intentId and clientSecret
User > Payment modal: card or UPI details
Payment modal > Mock gateway: confirm payment
Mock gateway > Mock gateway: judge the payment
Mock gateway > Webhook handler: signed event HMAC SHA256

alt [payment succeeded] {
  Webhook handler > SQLite: mark order paid and set paid_at
  Webhook handler > Mailer: send confirmation email
}
else [payment failed] {
  Webhook handler > SQLite: mark order failed so the user can retry
}

Mock gateway --> Payment modal: result message
loop [poll until paid] {
  Payment modal > Orders API: GET /orders/id
  Orders API --> Payment modal: paymentStatus
}
Payment modal --> User: success and open the order page
